<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>VIP Factor Screen — {{ symbol }}</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 900px; color: #222; line-height: 1.45; }
    h1, h2 { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; }
    th { background: #f3f3f3; }
    .meta { color: #555; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .caveat { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    img.importance { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #ddd; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Volatility Intelligence Platform — Factor Screen</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Symbol: <strong>{{ symbol }}</strong><br />
    Experiment: {{ experiment_id }}<br />
    Generated: {{ generated_on }}
  </p>

  <h2>Research question</h2>
  <p>
    Which features best predict next-5-day close-to-close realized volatility
    (<code>{{ target_column }}</code>) under walk-forward evaluation with primary
    metric <code>{{ primary_metric }}</code> (lower is better)?
  </p>

  <h2>Locked methodology</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Target: <code>{{ target_column }}</code></li>
    <li>Primary metric: <code>{{ primary_metric }}</code></li>
    <li>Walk-forward: expanding, n_splits={{ n_splits }}, embargo={{ embargo_size }}</li>
    <li>Screening model for importance: <code>{{ screening_model }}</code></li>
    <li>Importance: median ΔQLIKE under test-column permutation (mean reported too)</li>
    <li>Inference baseline: <code>{{ baseline_model }}</code></li>
    <li>Primary inference: block bootstrap of mean OOS ΔQLIKE
        (block length={{ bootstrap_block_length }},
        B={{ bootstrap_n_resamples }}, α={{ alpha }})</li>
    <li>Secondary inference: HLN–DM with Newey–West lags={{ nw_lags }}
        (not the primary significance claim)</li>
  </ul>

<h2>Model horse-race</h2>
<p class="meta">
  “Significantly lower” is used only when the primary block-bootstrap test
  rejects at α and mean ΔQLIKE favors the challenger. Otherwise use
  “lower / higher mean OOS QLIKE”. Fold-mean rankings alone are descriptive.
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>model</th>
      <th>qlike</th>
      <th>mse</th>
      <th>mae</th>
      <th>mean ΔQLIKE</th>
      <th>bootstrap CI</th>
      <th>bootstrap p</th>
      <th>HLN p</th>
      <th>vs HAR</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for row in model_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.model }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.qlike) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mse) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mae) }}</td>
      <td>
        {% if row.mean_delta_qlike is not none %}
          {{ "%.6f"|format(row.mean_delta_qlike) }}
        {% else %}—{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.bootstrap_ci_low is not none and row.bootstrap_ci_high is not none %}
          [{{ "%.6f"|format(row.bootstrap_ci_low) }},
           {{ "%.6f"|format(row.bootstrap_ci_high) }}]
        {% else %}—{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.bootstrap_pvalue is not none %}
          {{ "%.4f"|format(row.bootstrap_pvalue) }}
        {% else %}—{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.hln_pvalue is not none %}
          {{ "%.4f"|format(row.hln_pvalue) }}
        {% else %}—{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>{{ row.comparison_note }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Ranked factors</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>feature</th>
      <th>median_importance</th>
      <th>mean_importance</th>
      <th>std_importance</th>
      <th>top_k_hit_rate</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for row in factor_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.feature }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.median_importance) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mean_importance) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.std_importance) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "%.3f"|format(row.top_k_hit_rate) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>What works when</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>regime</th>
      <th>best_model</th>
      <th>qlike</th>
      <th>mse</th>
      <th>mae</th>
      <th>n_obs</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for row in regime_best_rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.regime }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.model }}</td>
      <td>
        {% if row.qlike is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.qlike) }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.mse is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mse) }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.mae is not none %}{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mae) }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>{{ row.n_obs }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

  <h2>Importance plot</h2>
  {% if importance_image_base64 %}
  <img class="importance"
       alt="Permutation importance bar chart"
       src="data:image/png;base64,{{ importance_image_base64 }}" />
  {% else %}
  <p>Importance plot unavailable.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for caveat in caveats %}
    <li class="caveat">{{ caveat }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</body>
</html>